1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Nearly 1 in 3 U.S. adults got under seven hours of sleep a day in 2024. Source: CDC and NCHS.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,500
Sleep hygiene means habits that help your body know bedtime is coming. Start small.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Start with your wake-up time. Keep it close to the same time most days.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Give yourself a dimmer, quieter hour before bed when you can.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:25,000
If caffeine keeps you up, move your last cup earlier.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,500
A cool, quiet, dark room is a good place to start.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:35,000
Pick one to try tonight. Save if useful. If sleep problems stick around, talk with a healthcare professional.
